  <prompt>Close the A-22 part of finding FR-17 (Low): LookupUserMembershipNodeExecutor passes IncludeRelated = new[] { "*" } under a stale "the resolver accepts-but-ignores in Phase 1A" comment — but the resolver no longer ignores it, so any playbook node with IncludeRelated = true now throws MembershipDepthExceededException (reason "unknown-entity") on every execution. Pass a valid related-entity argument (or none) so the node executes without throwing.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the AI playbook node-executor pipeline and the MembershipResolverService IncludeRelated contract. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>A playbook node configured with includeRelated: true executes without throwing; the executor passes an argument the resolver accepts (a concrete related-entity list, or null/omitted), and the stale comment is corrected.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Finding A-22 (10-finding-confirmations.md, PARTIAL — real failure, different exception reason than reported): LookupUserMembershipNodeExecutor.cs:231-234 sets IncludeRelated = (config.IncludeRelated ?? false) ? new[] { "*" } : null under the comment (:226-230) "the resolver accepts-but-ignores in Phase 1A." The resolver no longer ignores it: MembershipResolverService.ResolveAsync:164-185 pre-validates each IncludeRelated entry and throws MembershipDepthExceededException only for chain syntax (contains '.' or '/'); "*" passes pre-validation, flows into ResolveTransitiveAsync:957-978 → DiscoverLookupsTargetingAsync(relatedEntity:"*") → metadata fetch for entity "*" fails → InvalidOperationException → rethrown as MembershipDepthExceededException(reasonTag:"unknown-entity"). The executor's catch chain (:287-332) has no case for it → catch(Exception) (:318) → NodeOutput.Error(InternalError). Net: any node with includeRelated:true errors on every execution (InternalError). Functionality bug, no security impact. FR-17 acceptance: node executes without throwing.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/LookupUserMembershipNodeExecutor.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Membership/MembershipResolverService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/LookupUserMembershipNodeTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Characterization test (if 001 covered this node) pinning the throw; otherwise created here.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-034">Pass IncludeRelated values the resolver's contract accepts (concrete related-entity names, honoring the 1-hop cap), not a wildcard the metadata layer cannot resolve. Scope: the executor's IncludeRelated construction.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed on genuine errors, but a supported config (includeRelated:true) must NOT map to an unsupported resolver argument — correct the mapping, do not swallow the exception. Scope: the executor.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">If includeRelated:true has no well-defined related-entity set at this node, the correct behavior is to omit IncludeRelated (null), not to pass "*". Confirm the intended semantics before choosing. Scope: the mapping decision.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">BFF-touching task (CLAUDE.md §10): report publish size vs ~44.96 MB baseline in PR; ceiling 60 MB (NFR-06). Scope: this task's PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>membership node executor</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-034-user-record-membership.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/ai.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/investigation/10-finding-confirmations.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="membership-consumer" location=".claude/patterns/api/membership-consumer.md">Correct IncludeRelated usage by membership consumers</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load knowledge files; declare FULL rigor.</step>
    <step order="1">Read LookupUserMembershipNodeExecutor.cs:226-234 and the resolver's IncludeRelated pre-validation (MembershipResolverService.ResolveAsync:164-185, ResolveTransitiveAsync:957-978).</step>
    <step order="2">Decide the correct mapping for config.IncludeRelated == true: either a concrete related-entity list valid for this node, or null (omit) if no set is defined. Replace the ["*"] argument accordingly and correct the stale comment.</step>
    <step order="3">Author LookupUserMembershipNodeTests: a node with includeRelated:true executes without throwing and returns a NodeOutput (not InternalError); includeRelated:false is unchanged.</step>
    <step order="4">Run full test suite; build green.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="6">Document the mapping decision in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the product intent of includeRelated:true at this node is genuinely "all related entities" (which the resolver cannot express within the 1-hop cap), STOP and escalate — the feature may need a defined related-entity set rather than a silent null.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests — existing BFF test project; no test covers the LookupUserMembership node executor with includeRelated:true (A-22 was found by manual code read).</existing>
    <extension>Yes — a new test file inside the existing project; test surface for existing code, not new production surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the test, the node's runtime throw on includeRelated:true can regress, breaking any playbook branch that sets the flag (FR-17 A-22 part).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools><tool name="dotnet">Build + test</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/LookupUserMembershipNodeExecutor.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/LookupUserMembershipNodeTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A playbook node with includeRelated:true executes without throwing and returns a NodeOutput, not InternalError (FR-17 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A node with includeRelated:false behaves exactly as before (no regression).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the executor no longer passes "*" to the resolver (asserted by test or inspection).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit tests pass; build green; publish size reported in PR and ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-17 (A-22 part); A-15/A-16 parts are task 018. This is the only Phase 0 code task outside the contended external-access/auth directories — file-disjoint and parallel-safe with task 014 (group P0-B).

COMPLETED 2026-08-21: IncludeRelated now maps to null (not "*") when includeRelated:true — the node's
ConfigJson schema has no field for naming concrete related entities, so there is no well-defined set to
pass; null is the mapping the goal statement itself sanctions. All 4 stale "accepts-but-ignores"/"task 054
implements" comment locations corrected. Escalation trigger fired on inspection (original R3 task 041 intent
for includeRelated:true does look like it meant "all related entities", which the resolver cannot express)
— resolved by implementing the null mapping (satisfies FR-17's own acceptance wording) and flagging as an
open, non-blocking product-semantics question in notes/task-019-fix-lookup-membership-node-executor.md §3
(recommend a future relatedEntities:string[] config field, or removing the dead flag). New KEEP-path suite
at tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/LookupUserMembershipIncludeRelatedCharacterizationTests.cs
(4 tests) using a hand-written resolver double calibrated to throw on ANY non-empty IncludeRelated entry
(not a stub that always succeeds) — non-vacuity verified empirically by temporarily reverting the fix and
confirming 2/4 tests go red, then restoring and confirming 4/4 green. Also corrected 1 pre-existing test in
tests/unit/.../LookupUserMembershipNodeExecutorTests.cs that pinned the pre-fix buggy behavior (would have
broken on this fix otherwise) — not in the original file list, done because leaving it red is not a real
completion. Build green, 21/21 relevant tests + 86/86 full AccessControl namespace pass. Publish size 44.97
MB incl. PDBs (Δ +0.01 MB vs baseline). Step 9.5 gates (code-review + adr-check) run: 0 Critical, 0
Violations. Did NOT touch TASK-INDEX.md/current-task.md per orchestrator instruction (task 014 running
concurrently). Did NOT touch MembershipResolverService.cs (task 015) or CachedAccessDataSource.cs (task
014). Two stale-comment findings flagged out-of-scope for follow-up: MembershipEndpoints.cs and
IMembershipResolverService.cs both still say "ACCEPTED-BUT-IGNORED — task 054 implements" (false — task 054
shipped and the resolver does not ignore the value).</notes>

